# CODEOWNERS — multi-team review routing
#
# GitHub uses this file to auto-request reviews from the right team
# when a PR touches files matching the pattern. Order matters: LATER
# patterns override earlier ones (rightmost wins).
#
# To activate:
#   1. Rename .github/CODEOWNERS.suggested to .github/CODEOWNERS. The
#      bootstrap installs it as `.suggested` ON PURPOSE: an active
#      CODEOWNERS whose @teams don't exist in your org blocks EVERY PR
#      merge under branch protection. Fill in real teams/users below
#      FIRST, then rename. (`./manage.sh doctor` warns while it's still
#      `.suggested`.)
#   2. Configure branch protection on `main` to require review from
#      Code Owners. Settings → Branches → Branch protection rules →
#      Require review from Code Owners.
#   3. Each `@team-or-user` reference must exist in the org and have
#      write access to the repo.
#
# Syntax: <pattern> <space> <@user-or-team>+
#   - patterns are gitignore-style globs
#   - teams are `@org/team-name`
#   - users are `@username`
#   - multiple owners separated by space (any can approve)
#
# Customize the entries below. The defaults are placeholders.

# ---------- Default owner (catches everything not matched below) ----
*                               @your-org/maintainers

# ORDER MATTERS: GitHub uses the LAST matching rule. Broad rules go
# FIRST; the specific substrate rules below come LAST so they win for
# the agent/hook surfaces. (If you move the broad `/.github/` rule below
# `/.github/hooks/`, devops would silently own the hooks — a footgun.)

# ---------- CI / infra (broad — placed FIRST so specifics win) ------
/.github/                       @your-org/devops
/Dockerfile                     @your-org/devops
/docker-compose.yml             @your-org/devops

# ---------- Decisions + postmortems — architectural review ---------
/docs/decisions/                @your-org/architects
/docs/postmortems/              @your-org/architects @your-org/sre

# ---------- Substrate — change reviews (LAST so they override broad) -
# The substrate is load-bearing for every commit. Edits to it should
# get reviewed by the team that owns the discipline + at least one
# operator who runs the pipeline daily. Directory rules end in `/` so
# they cover nested files recursively (GitHub semantics).
/scripts/                       @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/tests/                         @your-org/substrate-maintainers
# Auditor-reference + architecture docs are agent-facing (read by the
# checklist-auditor, ultrareview, and on architecture work).
/docs/blind-spot-checklists/    @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/docs/templates/                @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/docs/ARCHITECTURE.md           @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/docs/INTENT.md                 @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/docs/README.md                 @your-org/substrate-maintainers
# UI design system — agent reads it on UI work (only if --ui yes).
/design-system/                 @your-org/frontend @your-org/design-system
# manage.sh is privileged: CI runs `./manage.sh setup|doctor|check`.
/manage.sh                      @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/pytest.ini                     @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.pre-commit-config.yaml        @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.gitattributes                 @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.gitignore                     @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.github/dependabot.yml         @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/AGENTS.md                      @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/CLAUDE.md                      @your-org/substrate-maintainers
# Agent-config + privileged-execution surfaces (hooks run with user perms).
/.substrate/                    @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.claude/                       @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.codex/                        @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.agents/                       @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.github/hooks/                 @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.github/instructions/          @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.github/workflows/             @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.github/copilot-instructions.md @your-org/substrate-maintainers
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @your-org/substrate-maintainers
# HISTORY is append-only (merge=union), but agents READ it at startup —
# so it is an agent-context surface and MUST be owned (an ownerless line
# here would override the catch-all via last-match and leave it unowned).
/docs/HISTORY.md                @your-org/substrate-maintainers @your-org/sre

# ---------- Project-specific source paths (CUSTOMIZE) ---------------
# Add patterns for your project's modules. Examples:
#   /src/auth/                    @your-org/auth-team
#   /src/billing/                 @your-org/billing-team
#   /apps/web/                    @your-org/frontend
#   /infra/terraform/             @your-org/devops
#   *.sql                         @your-org/data-platform
